### 3. TYPESCRIPT / INTERACTION CODE

**Primary Files:**

#### a) Scene Configuration & Text Animation
**File:** `resource/ts/pages/about/scene/about.scene.ts` (Lines 44-62, 337-344, 484-490)

**Gallery Scene Configuration:**
```typescript
const GALLERY_TEXT_SELECTOR = ".no-sub-about-gallery .is-block-reveal";
const aboutGalleryDomState = { visible: false, timers: [] as number[] };

// Scroll scene selector registration
const ABOUT_SCROLL_SCENE_SELECTORS: SceneSelectorMap<AboutSceneSectionKey> = {
  gallery: '.no-sub-about-gallery[data-scene="gallery"]',
};

// Gallery scroll progress config
const ABOUT_SCROLL_SCENE_OPTIONS: SceneProgressOptionsMap<AboutSceneSectionKey> = {
  gallery: {
    activationMode: "sectionTop",
    activationOffsetRatio: 0,
    progressMode: "top",
    scrollSpanVh: 200,
    progressLagMs: 280,
    progressStart: 0.04,
    progressEnd: 0.96,
    progressPower: 1.04,
  },
};

// Gallery scene event handlers
const scenes = {
  gallery: {
    onProgress: (progress: number): void => {
      syncSectionTextReveal(GALLERY_TEXT_SELECTOR, aboutGalleryDomState, progress);
    },
    onDispose: (): void => {
      disposeSectionTextReveal(GALLERY_TEXT_SELECTOR, aboutGalleryDomState);
    },
  },
};
```

**Text reveal logic** (Lines 159-188):
```typescript
const SECTION_TEXT_REVEAL_THRESHOLD = 0.18;
const SECTION_TEXT_HIDE_THRESHOLD = 0.08;
const SECTION_TEXT_STAGGER_MS = 150;

function syncSectionTextReveal(
  selector: string,
  domState: { visible: boolean; timers: number[] },
  progress: number,
): void {
  const shouldShow = progress >= SECTION_TEXT_REVEAL_THRESHOLD;
  const shouldHide = !shouldShow && progress < SECTION_TEXT_HIDE_THRESHOLD;
  if (!shouldShow && !shouldHide) return;
  if (domState.visible === shouldShow) return;
  domState.visible = shouldShow;
  domState.timers = clearTimers(domState.timers);
  const elements = Array.from(document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>(selector));
  elements.forEach((el, i) => {
    const id = window.setTimeout(() => {
      el.classList.toggle("is-block-reveal-up", shouldShow);
    }, i * SECTION_TEXT_STAGGER_MS);
    domState.timers.push(id);
  });
}
```

#### b) WebGL Canvas Renderer
**File:** `resource/ts/pages/about/render/InfiniteGalleryRenderer.ts` (Full file, 522 lines)

**Core Features:**
- **Class:** `InfiniteGalleryRenderer` — standalone Three.js WebGL renderer
- **Canvas:** Rendered to `#about-gallery-canvas` element
- **Gallery Images:** 8 unsplash.com images (Lines 28-37)
- **Rendering System:**
  - Perspective camera, scene with 12 visible planes
  - Custom shader materials (vertex + fragment GLSL)
  - Infinite scroll simulation with depth-based cycling

**Key Constants:**
```typescript
const DEPTH_RANGE = 50;
const VISIBLE_COUNT = 12;
const MAX_HORIZONTAL_OFFSET = 8;
const MAX_VERTICAL_OFFSET = 8;
const SCROLL_DAMPING = 0.95;
const IDLE_THRESHOLD_MS = 3000;
const MAX_SCROLL_VEL = 20.0;
const SCROLL_SPEED = 1.0;
```

**Shader Effects (VERTEX_SHADER):**
- Curve deformation based on `scrollForce`
- Cloth-like ripple effect from scroll velocity
- Flag-wave animation on hover
- 3D perspective transformation

**Shader Effects (FRAGMENT_SHADER):**
- Dynamic blur based on depth position (fade in/out)
- Opacity calculations: `FADE_IN_START (0.05)` → `FADE_IN_END (0.25)` → `FADE_OUT_START (0.4)` → `FADE_OUT_END (0.43)`
- Blur transitions: `BLUR_IN_START (0.0)` → `BLUR_IN_END (0.1)` → `BLUR_OUT_START (0.4)` → `BLUR_OUT_END (0.43)`

**Interaction Methods:**
- **Wheel scroll:** `_onWheel` — scroll velocity adjustment via deltaY
- **Keyboard:** `_onKeyDown` — Arrow keys for manual navigation
- **Touch:** `_onTouchStart`, `_onTouchMove` — touch drag velocity
- **Pointer:** `_onPointerMove`, `_onPointerLeave` — hover detection with raycasting for hover effects
- **Auto-play:** Starts after 3000ms idle, triggered by `_tickAutoPlay()` interval check

**Lifecycle:**
```typescript
async init(canvas: HTMLCanvasElement): Promise<void>
  - Texture loading (7 images + 1 fallback = 8 total)
  - Plane geometry creation (12 instances)
  - Event listener attachment
  - ResizeObserver & IntersectionObserver for visibility/responsive sizing
  - Auto-play interval (100ms ticks)

dispose(): void
  - Geometry/material/texture cleanup
  - Renderer.dispose() + forceContextLoss()
  - Event listener removal
  - Observer disconnection
```

#### c) Page Runtime Integration
**File:** `resource/ts/pages/about/runtime/AboutPageRuntime.ts` (Lines 7-49)

```typescript
export class AboutPageRuntime implements IPageRuntime {
  private _galleryRenderer: InfiniteGalleryRenderer | null = null;

  async init(root?: ParentNode | null): Promise<void> {
    const galleryCanvas = (root ?? document).querySelector<HTMLCanvasElement>(
      `#${GALLERY_CANVAS_ID}`,
    );
    if (galleryCanvas instanceof HTMLCanvasElement) {
      this._galleryRenderer?.dispose();
      this._galleryRenderer = new InfiniteGalleryRenderer();
      await this._galleryRenderer.init(galleryCanvas);
    }
  }

  dispose(): void {
    this._galleryRenderer?.dispose();
    this._galleryRenderer = null;
  }
}
```

**Integration:**
- Instantiates and initializes `InfiniteGalleryRenderer` on page load
- Queries canvas by ID: `#about-gallery-canvas`
- Handles lifecycle (init/dispose)

---

### 4. SUMMARY: VISUAL & INTERACTIVE BEHAVIOR

**Visual Appearance:**
- Full-viewport sticky section that spans 200% height (scroll-anchored)
- 3D infinite scrolling gallery with 8 rotating images rendered via Three.js
- Images are 3D planes positioned in depth space with curved/wavy deformation
- Dark gradient overlay (bottom 60%) with white text at bottom of viewport
- Text: "우리는 당신의 브랜드 개발 디자인 여정을 리드한다" (We lead your brand development, design journey) + subtext
- Images fade in/out and blur dynamically as they traverse the depth range
- Grab cursor on canvas indicates interactivity

**Interactive Behavior:**
1. **Scroll Input:** Wheel, arrow keys, and touch swipe adjust scroll velocity with damping (95% frame damping)
2. **Hover Detection:** Raycaster detects which image is hovered; hovered image plays flag-wave shader animation
3. **Auto-play:** After 3000ms idle, gallery auto-scrolls upward at constant acceleration
4. **Responsive:** Canvas resizes with ResizeObserver; stops rendering when scrolled out of view (IntersectionObserver)
5. **Text Animation:** Headline and subtext reveal (`.is-block-reveal-up` class) when scroll progress enters gallery section (≥18% progress), with 150ms stagger between text lines

**Scroll Integration:**
- Section is tracked by Theatre.js as scene key `"gallery"`
- Progress tracked over 200vh scroll span with 280ms lag and 1.04 power curve
- Progress threshold (18%) triggers staggered text reveal
- Background shader state changes to `aboutHeroSlogan` variant for this section

