This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.

Summary:
1. Primary Request and Intent:

The user established the assistant as a "web interaction expert" role for the NINEONELABS renewal project at `c:\Users\edn_y\renew_nineonelabs`. Sequential feature requests were made for the About page:

**Gallery section (`no-sub-about-gallery`):**
- Center text in viewport (화면 가운데 맞춤)
- Text starts hidden, reveals on scroll (using existing `is-block-reveal` pattern)
- Gallery starts moving at the same time as text reveals (scroll-synchronized)
- Add scroll hold buffer (extra 100svh after interaction ends before proceeding to next section)

**Proof section (`no-sub-about-proof`):**
- Same text centering as gallery
- Add a second sentence to the section
- Two-stage sequential text reveal: first text shows → disappears → second text appears
- Remove camera zoom-in effect (planes getting closer while scrolling)
- Scroll velocity → faster ring rotation (not just progress-based)
- Same 100svh hold buffer as gallery

**Most recent request (PENDING):**
- Abandon the JS scroll-threshold + timer approach for proof text reveal
- Use CSS `position: sticky` or `fixed` approach instead
- User's exact words: "해당 방법말고 scss sticky 방법으로 처리해줘 혹은 fixed방식으로 글씨 보여지고 사라지고 그 다음 글씨 보여지고 현 구조에서는 그 방식이 베스트일거같음"

2. Key Technical Concepts:
- **Three.js WebGL renderers**: `InfiniteGalleryRenderer` (gallery canvas), `AboutProofRenderer` (proof rings canvas)
- **`position: sticky` scroll pattern**: `min-height: Nsvh` container + `position: sticky; top: 0; height: 100svh` inner wrapper
- **`is-block-reveal` CSS system**: `opacity: 0; visibility: hidden; transform: translate3d(0, 18px, 0); filter: blur(8px)` → toggled to visible via `is-block-reveal-up` class
- **`--transition-slow: 0.6s`** (`var(--duration-slow) var(--ease-smooth)`)
- **Scroll progress callbacks**: `registerProofProgressCallback`, `registerGalleryProgressCallback` pattern in `about.scene.ts`
- **Scene progress system**: `onProgress(progress: number)` + `onDispose()` callbacks per scroll section
- **`scrollSpanVh: 200`** for both gallery and proof — progress 0→1 over 200svh
- **`min-height: 300svh`** (changed from 200svh) — adds 100svh hold buffer after progress reaches 1.0
- **`syncRevealBounded`** — custom helper for bounded progress-range reveals with optional `enterDelayMs`
- **CSS scroll-driven animations** (`animation-timeline: view()`) — proposed approach for CSS-only reveal
- **`IntersectionObserver`** — mentioned as alternative reliable approach

3. Files and Code Sections:

**`resource/scss/pages/_sub.scss`** (lines 509-620):
- Gallery section changed: `min-height: 300svh`, `justify-content: center`, `align-items: center`, `text-align: center`, `background: radial-gradient(ellipse 90% 55% at 50% 50%, rgba(0,0,0,0.55) 0%, transparent 100%)`
- Proof section changed: same centering + gradient changes, `min-height: 300svh`, removed `__sub` rule
- Current proof structure still uses `__sticky` / `__content` / `__canvas-wrap` pattern (pending restructure)

**`resource/ts/pages/about/scene/about.scene.ts`** (key sections):
- Added `registerGalleryProgressCallback` export + `_galleryProgressCallback`
- Changed proof selectors: `PROOF_HEADLINE_SELECTOR = ".no-sub-about-proof__content .no-sub-about-proof__headline.is-block-reveal:first-child"`, `PROOF_SUB_SELECTOR = ".no-sub-about-proof__content .no-sub-about-proof__headline.is-block-reveal:last-child"`
- Current constants: `PROOF_STAGE_SPLIT = 0.42`, `PROOF_SUB_SHOW = 0.68`
- Added `syncRevealBounded` helper:
```ts
function syncRevealBounded(
  selector: string,
  domState: { visible: boolean; timers: number[] },
  shouldShow: boolean,
  shouldHide: boolean,
  enterDelayMs = 0,
): void {
  if (!shouldShow && !shouldHide) return;
  if (domState.visible === shouldShow) return;
  domState.visible = shouldShow;
  domState.timers = clearTimers(domState.timers);
  const baseDelay = shouldShow ? enterDelayMs : 0;
  const elements = Array.from(document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>(selector));
  elements.forEach((el, i) => {
    const id = window.setTimeout(() => {
      el.classList.toggle("is-block-reveal-up", shouldShow);
    }, baseDelay + i * SECTION_TEXT_STAGGER_MS);
    domState.timers.push(id);
  });
}
```
- Current proof `onProgress` handler:
```ts
proof: {
  onProgress: (progress: number): void => {
    const hShow = progress >= SECTION_TEXT_REVEAL_THRESHOLD && progress < PROOF_STAGE_SPLIT;
    const hHide = !hShow && (progress < SECTION_TEXT_HIDE_THRESHOLD || progress >= PROOF_STAGE_SPLIT);
    syncRevealBounded(PROOF_HEADLINE_SELECTOR, aboutProofHeadlineDomState, hShow, hHide);
    const sShow = progress >= PROOF_SUB_SHOW;
    const sHide = !sShow && progress < PROOF_SUB_SHOW - 0.06;
    syncRevealBounded(PROOF_SUB_SELECTOR, aboutProofSubDomState, sShow, sHide, 900);
    _proofProgressCallback?.(progress);
  },
  onDispose: (): void => {
    disposeSectionTextReveal(PROOF_HEADLINE_SELECTOR, aboutProofHeadlineDomState);
    disposeSectionTextReveal(PROOF_SUB_SELECTOR, aboutProofSubDomState);
    _proofProgressCallback?.(0);
  },
},
```

**`resource/ts/pages/about/render/InfiniteGalleryRenderer.ts`**:
- Added `GALLERY_ENABLE_THRESHOLD = 0.18`
- Added `private _galleryEnabled = false`
- Added `setScrollProgress(p: number)` method
- Modified `_tickAutoPlay()` to guard on `_galleryEnabled`

**`resource/ts/pages/about/render/AboutProofRenderer.ts`**:
- Added `private _scrollDelta = 0`
- Updated `setScrollProgress()`:
```ts
setScrollProgress(progress: number): void {
  const prev = this._scrollProgress;
  this._scrollProgress = Math.max(0, Math.min(1, progress));
  this._scrollDelta = Math.abs(this._scrollProgress - prev);
}
```
- Updated `_tick()`:
  - Removed: `this._camera.position.z = 22 - p * 6` (zoom-in effect)
  - Added: `this._scrollDelta *= 0.88; const velocityBoost = this._scrollDelta * 100; const speed = ROTATION_SPEED_Y * (1 + p * 1.8 + velocityBoost);`

**`resource/ts/pages/about/runtime/AboutPageRuntime.ts`**:
- Import updated to include `registerGalleryProgressCallback`
- Added callback wiring after gallery renderer init

**`views/pages/about/index.php`** (proof section, lines 207-214):
- Current state (user modified): two `<h2 class="no-sub-about-proof__headline f-display-1 is-block-reveal">` elements
```html
